meta {
  name: demo 0.2.0
  seq: 1
}

auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{demoKey}}
}

docs {
  The scenario of `scripts/demo-e2e.sh`, one request at a time. Select the
  environment **demo-0.2.0** and start the demo stack:

  ```
  make demo        # or: scripts/demo-e2e.sh with KEEP=1
  ```

  The keys (`demoKey`, `financeKey`) are public and for the demo only. The
  requests run in order; 02, 03 and 07 keep the decision id of the
  answer in `ibanDecisionId`, `refusedDecisionId` and `shadowDecisionId`.

  What HTTP cannot show (the decision records in PostgreSQL) is given as
  commands in the docs of the requests concerned.

  The audit chain is sealed every 100 records. After enough requests, check
  it with the public key of the demo (`docker compose ... run --rm audit-key`
  prints it):

  ```
  docker compose -f deploy/compose/docker-compose.yml exec tavian /app verify-audit -public-key ed25519:...
  ```
}
